# certificate-signer's own Trivy allowlist -- kept separate from the parent
# monolith's .trivyignore (repo root) because this image's exposure profile
# is different: certificate-signer is deliberately public-facing
# (Cloudflare-fronted -- see chameleon-paper/TEE_ATTESTATION_PLAN.md's
# Phase 2 networking decision), unlike the parent's
# INGRESS_TRAFFIC_INTERNAL_ONLY posture. Reusing the parent file's "not
# reachable from untrusted clients" reasoning would be actively misleading
# here -- every entry below is justified on its own terms for this image.

# node:22-alpine's own OpenSSL packages (libcrypto3/libssl3) -- no fix
# published upstream yet as of 2026-08-31: the current node:22-alpine tag's
# digest already matches what Dockerfile.certificate-signer pins, so there
# is no newer base image available to re-pin to right now. Re-check on the
# next periodic base-image re-pin (see that Dockerfile's own comment on
# this discipline, and Phase 1's reasoning for why apk update/upgrade is
# deliberately not run here instead).
CVE-2026-14456

# ip-address, pacote, tar -- npm's own bundled copy inside node:22-alpine
# (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/), same class of finding the parent
# .trivyignore documents for other npm-internal CVEs (different CVE IDs,
# same root cause). Confirmed via `npm ls ip-address/pacote/tar` in this
# directory: none of these three are actual dependencies of this module
# (all resolve empty) -- and this image's CMD
# (`node dist/certificate-signer/entrypoint.js`) never invokes npm at
# runtime.
CVE-2026-69192
CVE-2026-9496
CVE-2026-73566

# brace-expansion -- IS a real dependency here (confirmed via `npm ls
# --all`: @google-cloud/firestore -> google-gax@3.6.1 -> protobufjs-cli@1.1.1
# -> glob@8.1.0 -> minimatch@5.1.9 -> brace-expansion), unlike the three
# above. protobufjs-cli provides the pbjs/pbts .proto-to-JS codegen CLI (its
# own dependencies -- jsdoc, escodegen, espree -- confirm it's a
# documentation/codegen toolchain, not a runtime library) -- google-gax
# lists it as a direct dependency for an optional compileProtos step this
# module never invokes. This module's runtime code only imports
# protobufjs's message encode/decode APIs via google-gax's gRPC transport,
# never protobufjs-cli's CLI, so glob/minimatch/brace-expansion's actual
# code never executes in this image.
CVE-2026-69152
